.TH DEADHEAT 1 "2026-11-27" "deadheat 0.1.0" "Spectacle Line Manual"
.SH NAME
deadheat \- two-lane coding agent duel runner, close-call adjudicator, and series analytics tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdeadheat\fR [\fB-h\fR | \fB--help\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIFILE\fR ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBdeadheat\fR races two competing model attempts at one task in isolated workspace directories, decides the winner from suite pass/fail status, elapsed wall-clock seconds, optional handicaps, and the fixed five-percent close-call band, salvages defeated patches, and prints thirty-five offline analytical readings across races, standings, series, and championships.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBrun <spec.json>\fR
Execute a two-lane local duel specification and write the version 1 race record.
.TP
\fBrace [--standings <standings.json>] <race.json>\fR
Score a recorded race and optionally update cumulative model standings.
.TP
\fBclosecall <race.json>\fR
Print close-call adjudication or dual-judge panel details for a race.
.TP
\fBadopt | discard <race.json> <patches_dir>\fR
Write or remove archived loser patch files for a decided race.
.TP
\fBstandings <standings.json>\fR
Render cumulative wins, losses, no-results, and token totals.
.TP
\fBseries <series.json>\fR
Render a first-to-N race series.
.TP
\fBflip <series.json>\fR
Compare each race's scratch winner against its handicap-adjusted winner (flipped, held, or no result).
.TP
\fBchampionship | totals | pairing <championship.json>\fR
Summarize multi-series championships, aggregate model totals, and head-to-head pairings.
.TP
\fBcomeback | distance | rally | deadlock | streak | cluster | closing | opening | turns | lead | crossings | tenure | depths | spells | reigns | place | peak | recovery | laststand | firststand | firststrike | firstreign | lastreign | leadchanges | outset | tail | crosshead <championship.json>\fR
Run the twenty-seven trajectory, momentum, reign, and deficit championship readings.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\fB0\fR
Race executed cleanly (run), patch adopted or discarded (adopt or discard), or report printed cleanly.
.TP
\fB1\fR
Malformed JSON refused with structured defect lines on stdout, unreadable or non-UTF-8 input file, existing workspace directory or malformed attempt result on run, 4300-digit integer overflow, adopt or discard invoked on a valid race with no winner, filesystem write failure, or closed stdout pipe on large output (>= 8192 bytes).
.TP
\fB2\fR
Unknown subcommand, unrecognized option, or wrong argument count on stderr.
.TP
\fB120\fR
Failed stderr stream write, or closed stdout pipe on short output (<= 4096 bytes).
.SH EXAMPLES
Score a recorded race
.nf
.RS 4
deadheat race examples/shadow-wins.json
.RE
.fi
.PP
Summarize model totals across a championship
.nf
.RS 4
deadheat totals examples/championship.json
.RE
.fi
.PP
Inspect comeback series across a championship
.nf
.RS 4
deadheat comeback examples/championship.json
.RE
.fi
